(* Pia.Core.Order (ADR 0040): every goal of the module is proved: the
   generic functions at each integer type, the laws of Eq and Ord for each
   type that meets them, and each instance's interface contract.
// RUN: FileCheck %s < %S/../../lib/Pia/Core/order.goals
// RUN: piac --emit=interface -o %t %S/../../lib/Pia/Core/Order.pia
// RUN: FileCheck --check-prefix=OPS %s < %t/Pia.Core.Order.Ops.piai
// RUN: FileCheck --check-prefix=CMP %s < %t/Pia.Core.Order.Compare.piai
*)

(* The laws are proved for each type, and lexicographical_compare meets its
   definition over every Ord t, once [generic]; its instance at each of
   the 8 integer types is discharged by that proof (ADR 0043). compare and
   the three-way comparison, which return an ordering, are proved at their
   instances.
// CHECK-NOT: failed
// CHECK-DAG: proved: 'lex_compare<u8>' is an instance of the generic proof of 'lex_compare' [generic]
// CHECK-DAG: proved: 'lex_compare<i64>' is an instance of the generic proof of 'lex_compare' [generic]
// CHECK-DAG: proved: the measure of 'lex_from<t>' decreases [generic]
// CHECK-DAG: not proved generically: 'compare' is proved at each instance, since it returns a value of ordering [generic]
// CHECK: 525 proved, 0 failed, 0 skipped
*)

